  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/can1357/oh-my-pi/tarball/v18.12.1",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/can1357/oh-my-pi/zipball/v18.12.1",
  "body": "## @oh-my-pi/pi-ai\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed every request failing behind a TLS-inspecting proxy that refuses compressed uploads: a 400/403/415 whose body is not JSON, or the Anthropic API's \"request body is not valid JSON\" after a proxy drops `Content-Encoding`, now resends the body uncompressed and stops compressing for that host ([#16108](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16108) by [@alphastorm](https://github.com/alphastorm))\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-catalog\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Anthropic's `request-encoding-rejection` now also matches the API's \"request body is not valid JSON\" 400, which a gzip body gets when a proxy drops its `Content-Encoding` header ([#16108](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16108) by [@alphastorm](https://github.com/alphastorm))\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent\n\n### Breaking Changes\n\n- Removed `display()` from eval in both Python and JavaScript; `print` (and `console.log` in JavaScript) covers it\n\n### Added\n\n- Added `advisor.continueSeverity` (`nit`, `concern`, `blocker`) to choose the minimum advisor note severity that wakes the agent after it finished with a final answer; lower-severity notes stay as a card at the end of the transcript\n- Printed DataFrames/Series render as tables, large dicts/lists and objects as JSON trees, and Markdown objects as Markdown for the user, while the model sees the printed text\n- Printing a figure or image in eval attaches the image to the result\n\n### Changed\n\n- An advisor `concern` raised after the agent's final answer now continues the run by default instead of waiting at the end of the transcript; set `advisor.continueSeverity` to `blocker` for the previous behavior\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed context-file `@` imports failing to load paths containing backslash-escaped spaces ([#16090](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/issues/16090))\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-natives\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed native memory growing without bound, and eventually crashing the process, when files in a downloaded (WASM) grammar language such as C# were parsed repeatedly ([#16067](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/issues/16067))\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-tui\n\n### Breaking Changes\n\n- `numberedCode`, `readContentCode` and `nativeDiff` take the file's path (`path`) instead of a language, and `describeGroupedOutput` drops its `lang` option: Tern picks the grammar of file contents from their path\n\n### Changed\n\n- Advisor notes in Tern read as a callout tinted by their worst severity: its icon and a tally (`Concern`, `1 blocker · 2 concerns`) head the card with the advisor's name at the end, and several notes each lead with their own severity icon\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed images rendering blank inside tmux on Kitty-capable terminals when tmux's `allow-passthrough` is off (the default); omp now falls back to SIXEL or the text placeholder instead of sending Kitty graphics tmux drops\n- Fixed Tern drawing tool cards' file contents (write, read, edit, grep, find, ast-grep, ast-edit) plain or in the wrong language when omp did not know the file's extension (`.ptx`) or mapped it to a neighbor (`.cu` as C++); omp now sends the file's path and Tern picks the grammar\n\n\n## What's Changed\n* fix(ai): resend uncompressed when a proxy rejects a compressed request body by @alphastorm in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16108\n* fix(tui): answered allow-passthrough in fake tmux client fixture by @roboomp in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16112\n* fix(ast): retired per-thread wasm parser store after a byte budget by @roboomp in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16078\n* fix(coding-agent): support escaped spaces in context imports by @roboomp in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/16091\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/compare/v18.12.0...v18.12.1",
